# Knowledge-sync secrets — local convenience for `npm run sync:internal` / `npm run sync:wiki`.
#
# ⚠ DO NOT `cp` THIS FILE OVER AN EXISTING `.env.sync.local`. It holds several unrelated
# secrets, and copying replaces ALL of them with placeholders — silently, since nothing
# reads them until a sync 401s hours later. That happened on 2026-08-24: the knowledge sync
# ran on a post-merge hook and returned `errors=149 rows=0` with Donny's RAG left stale.
# There is no backup; every key has to be fetched from the dashboard again.
# Check first (`ls .env.sync.local`), and append or edit single lines rather than copying.
#
# Setup (pick ONE; you don't need both):
#   A) If `.env.sync.local` does NOT exist, copy this file to it (same folder) and fill in
#      the values. It's gitignored, so it never gets committed.
#   B) OR skip the file and export the vars in your shell profile. An exported var always
#      wins over this file — and unlike this file, which is per-directory, it works from
#      every one of the 30+ worktrees.
#
# DONNY_SYNC_URL defaults to the prod endpoint, so you normally only need the key.
# To sync to staging instead, set DONNY_SYNC_URL here (or in your shell) to the
# staging functions URL.

# The PRODUCTION **service_role** key — despite this variable's name, it is NOT an
# `sb_secret_…` key. This line read `sb_secret_REPLACE_ME` until 2026-08-24, which sends you
# after the wrong credential: `donny-knowledge-sync` authorizes against `AIOS_INGEST_SECRET`,
# and prod has that set to the service-role key's value. Proven without reading either
# secret — `supabase secrets list` returns a SHA-256 of each, and the two digests are
# identical. (`_shared/ingest-auth.ts` says the ingest secret *should* be an `sb_secret_…`
# key so a rotation of the injected service-role key can't 401 these routines. That is the
# intended design and it was never actually done. If someone does it, change this line too.)
#
#   Supabase dashboard → the PROD project → Project Settings → API → service_role
#
# Verify you grabbed the right one BEFORE running a sync, without pasting it anywhere:
#   printf '%s' "<the key>" | shasum -a 256
# must print 9dfa8c1a2fe88648930d12310686f7cdabb3bbcf864ab64b016963312ff7b190
# (re-read the digest with `npx supabase secrets list --project-ref <ref>` if it ever rotates).
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# DONNY_SYNC_URL=https://zocahiffooqdybdhguqv.supabase.co/functions/v1/donny-knowledge-sync

# ── Staging headless login (`npm run staging:login`) ────────────────────────────────
# The STAGING service-role key — a DIFFERENT project from the key above
# (dragoncandy-staging, ref mhffqrawgizhprbobcta; the key above is PRODUCTION).
#   Supabase dashboard → dragoncandy-staging → Project Settings → API → service_role
#
# This lets an agent mint a session for a seeded staging test account without anyone
# typing a password, so verifying auth-gated screens no longer needs the founder.
# staging-login.mjs refuses to run if this value looks like the prod key.
STAGING_SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_ME

# ── Running SQL (`npm run db:query` / `npm run db:apply`) ───────────────────────────
# A Supabase PERSONAL ACCESS TOKEN — a different credential from every key above.
# Those are project keys; this one is a token for YOUR Supabase ACCOUNT, and it can
# reach every project your account can. Treat it accordingly.
#
#   Create at: https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
#   Starts with `sbp_`.
#
# Why it exists: this repo had no way to run SQL at all. `supabase db push` is banned
# here (the ledger has diverged by 200+ files, so a push re-runs them against prod),
# the CLI has no `db execute`, psql is not installed, and the Supabase MCP's OAuth
# returns "Unrecognized client_id". So a migration had to be pasted into the dashboard
# by hand, and schema facts were checked by probing PostgREST for
# column-does-not-exist errors instead of just querying pg_proc.
#
# An exported SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN in your shell wins over this file — and unlike
# this file, it works from every worktree, since this file lives per-directory.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_REPLACE_ME
